From: medyma <aneylovemzy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 23:16:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6.6 v8] net: sfp: opt in to warm-reboot recovery

Some modules stay powered across a warm reboot but stop answering I2C.
The warm-boot-recovery DT property opts a cage in: wait up to 10x300ms for
passive EEPROM readiness, then optionally power-cycle, pulse TX_DISABLE
(hold then release before I2C recovery), and retry. Enabled only on affected
BPI-R4 cages.

Signed-off-by: medyma <aneylovemzy@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/sff,sfp.yaml |  14 ++
 .../dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dts   |   2 +
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4.dts  |   5 +
 drivers/net/phy/sfp.c                                              | 156 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 177 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/sff,sfp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/sff,sfp.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/sff,sfp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/sff,sfp.yaml
@@ -54,6 +54,20 @@ properties:
       GPIO phandle and a specifier of the Transmitter Disable output gpio
       signal, active (Tx disable) high
 
+  power-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      GPIO phandle and a specifier of the module power output gpio. The active
+      state powers the module.
+
+  warm-boot-recovery:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Enable disruptive startup recovery only for SFP cages affected by modules
+      whose EEPROM can remain unavailable after a warm reboot. When a module is
+      present, the driver waits for passive EEPROM readiness before attempting
+      an optional power cycle, a TX_DISABLE pulse, or I2C bus recovery.
+
   "rate-select0-gpios":
     maxItems: 1
     description:
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dts
@@ -102,6 +102,7 @@
 		mod-def0-gpios = <&pio 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 		tx-disable-gpios = <&pio 21 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		maximum-power-milliwatt = <3000>;
